    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_50daf41fe705f1a8a26f273eb934550270263c8012ea3fddf9606c56c4ca3653",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The resonance proof keeps three burdens separate. An oscillatory estimate controls the excluded low-height interval by splitting near and separated logarithmic frequencies; Fourier decay and local cluster counting bound the denominator moment M_1; and a finite zeta approximation plus positivity reconstructs the GCD quantity inside the numerator M_2. These proved estimates make the moment ratio succeed. The concluding source remark then diagnoses, tentatively and only for this Soundararajan-style architecture, a remaining restriction from resonator-support capacity together with the available GCD upper bound, suggesting that the method can improve only the constant modestly.",
